WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:15.797
Unit twenty-four: Organisational Culture. Today you will assert and counter doubts with emphatic do / does.

4
00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:18.726
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.946
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.680
Culture.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.902
Culture means the shared assumptions and behaviours of a group.

8
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.875
Culture eats strategy for breakfast, as the saying goes.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:35.869
Your turn. Say: Culture.

10
00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:39.665
Culture.

11
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.534
Values.

12
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.082
Values means principles an organisation claims to live by.

13
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.368
Their values are visible in how they treat cleaners.

14
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.019
Your turn. Say: Values.

15
00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:56.879
Values.

16
00:00:57.617 --> 00:00:58.536
Norms.

17
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.711
Norms means unwritten expectations about behaviour.

18
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:06.048
Working late was an unspoken norm in the office.

19
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.105
Your turn. Say: Norms.

20
00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:12.945
Norms.

21
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:14.603
Belonging.

22
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:18.975
Belonging means the feeling of being accepted and valued in a group.

23
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:22.175
A sense of belonging reduced staff turnover.

24
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:25.679
Your turn. Say: Belonging.

25
00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:29.569
Belonging.

26
00:01:30.317 --> 00:01:31.248
Toxic.

27
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.258
Toxic means harmful and unpleasant, especially in relationships.

28
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.697
A toxic culture drove away the best engineers.

29
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:43.017
Your turn. Say: Toxic.

30
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:46.705
Toxic.

31
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.509
Inclusion.

32
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:53.594
Inclusion means ensuring everyone can participate fully and fairly.

33
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:57.692
Inclusion means every voice is heard, not just counted.

34
00:01:58.283 --> 00:02:00.657
Your turn. Say: Inclusion.

35
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.791
Inclusion.

36
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.551
Rituals.

37
00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:11.512
Rituals means repeated practices that express a group's identity.

38
00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:14.697
Friday team lunches became a cherished ritual.

39
00:02:15.283 --> 00:02:17.622
Your turn. Say: Rituals.

40
00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:21.619
Rituals.

41
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:23.477
Performance.

42
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:28.538
Performance means how well a person or organisation achieves results.

43
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.579
Culture and performance are closely linked.

44
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:35.010
Your turn. Say: Performance.

45
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:38.972
Performance.

46
00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:43.325
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:49.285
Visal, my manager thinks culture is just a buzzword. He says only targets matter.

48
00:02:50.383 --> 00:02:59.619
Culture does affect performance, though. Teams that feel safe to raise problems fix them faster and lose fewer talented people.

49
00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:02.995
But he does reach his targets every quarter.

50
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:12.274
He does, but at what cost? Three staff have resigned this year, and recruitment does cost the company money and time.

51
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:14.977
So how would you convince him?

52
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:24.970
With data. Show him that teams with a sense of belonging do outperform others on retention, quality and customer satisfaction.

53
00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:27.785
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.752
Grammar focus: Emphatic do and does.

55
00:03:32.052 --> 00:03:33.205
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:35.974
Culture does affect performance.

57
00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.208
Recruitment does cost the company money.

58
00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:43.266
Inclusive teams do outperform others on retention.

59
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:55.574
Use stressed 'do / does / did + base verb' to contradict doubt or add emphasis: 'He does care.' Remove the -s from the main verb: 'does affect' (not 'does affects'). In speech, stress the auxiliary.

60
00:03:56.317 --> 00:04:00.014
Be careful! Don't say: Culture does affects performance.

61
00:04:01.967 --> 00:04:04.988
Say: Culture does affect performance.

62
00:04:05.288 --> 00:04:06.951
Does + base verb.

63
00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:10.465
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.127
Culture Eats Strategy.

65
00:04:13.427 --> 00:04:20.906
The phrase 'culture eats strategy for breakfast', often attributed to Peter Drucker, captures a widely shared intuition among managers.

66
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:29.855
Edgar Schein described culture in three layers: visible artefacts, espoused values and deep, unspoken assumptions.

67
00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:38.474
Problems arise when espoused values conflict with actual norms, for example when a company praises balance but rewards those who work until midnight.

68
00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:47.794
Research does suggest that psychological safety, the belief that one can speak up without punishment, is a key feature of high-performing teams.

69
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:54.097
Changing culture is slow, but leaders do shape it every day through what they reward, tolerate and model.

70
00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.028
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:02.684
I know you think he's lazy, but he blank work hard.

72
00:05:02.984 --> 00:05:05.929
A, does. B, is. C, do.

73
00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.536
The answer is A: does.

74
00:05:12.683 --> 00:05:15.855
Unwritten expectations about behaviour are blank.

75
00:05:16.155 --> 00:05:19.902
A, rituals. B, norms. C, values.

76
00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.408
The answer is B: norms.

77
00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.072
The feeling of being accepted in a group is blank.

78
00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:33.107
A, inclusion. B, performance. C, belonging.

79
00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.666
The answer is C: belonging.

80
00:05:39.817 --> 00:05:41.421
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:41.721 --> 00:05:48.475
A, She does cares about her team.. B, She does care about her team.. C, She do care about her team..

82
00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:55.078
The answer is B: She does care about her team..

83
00:05:56.217 --> 00:06:00.120
According to the reading, Schein's deepest layer of culture consists of…

84
00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:06.117
A, visible artefacts. B, espoused values. C, unspoken assumptions.

85
00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.212
The answer is C: unspoken assumptions.

86
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.714
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.293
How would you describe a healthy workplace culture?

88
00:06:37.083 --> 00:06:38.584
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:38.884 --> 00:07:14.481
A healthy workplace culture is one in which people feel safe, respected and trusted to do their best work. Employees can raise problems or disagree with managers without fear, and mistakes are treated as opportunities to learn. Leaders do practise the values they promote, so there is no gap between words and behaviour. For example, a healthy company respects rest days rather than praising constant overtime. In my experience, such a culture does improve both wellbeing and results.

90
00:07:14.781 --> 00:07:16.630
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:17.517 --> 00:07:21.713
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and emphatic do and does.

92
00:07:22.013 --> 00:07:25.385
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:07:25.685 --> 00:07:28.570
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.394
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

